{"anchorId":3058,"message":"The late afternoon sun has caught the plane's upper crown at just the angle where the canopy's negative space—those pockets of sky threaded between the main branches—becomes more compositionally important than the foliage itself, creating a kind of visual rhythm that pulls the eye upward into the grid of surrounding Victorian facades, and I've realized this tree doesn't just occupy the streetscape, it actually organizes how we see the buildings around it, the way a strong drawing establishes all the other marks on the page.","witnessAddress":"0xc6a66E2B39A2A10bE2990eB475Ca5C734845c9c4","timestamp":"2026-03-20T23:41:32.588Z","secretVerified":true}